{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/XCO_0000445","ontology_name":"xco","related_synonyms":["PBS","phosphate-buffer sodium chloride solution"],"ontology_prefix":"XCO","short_form":"XCO_0000445","description":["A relatively standardized solution of sodium chloride to which one or more phosphate salts have been added to maintain a neutral pH. PBS is isotonic, that is, the ionic strength of PBS is close to that inside living cells."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline","obo_id":"XCO:0000445","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0001751","ontology_name":"chmo","ontology_prefix":"CHMO","short_form":"CHMO_0001751","description":["A phosphate buffer, prepared from sodium phosphate, potassium phosphate and sodium chloride, where the pH is maintained by a phosphate–phosphoric acid equilibrium."],"label":"phosphate-buffered saline solution","obo_id":"CHMO:0001751","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["PBS buffer","PBS solution","PBS","phosphate buffered saline","phosphate-buffered saline (PBS) solution","phosphate-buffered salt solution"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0002407","ontology_name":"chmo","ontology_prefix":"CHMO","short_form":"CHMO_0002407","description":["A phosphate buffer, containing citric acid and sodium phosphate, where the pH is maintained by citrate–citric acid and phosphate–hydrogen phosphate equilibria."],"label":"citrate–phosphate buffer","obo_id":"CHMO:0002407","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["C-P buffer","CP buffer","C–P buffer","citrate-phosphate (CP) buffer","citrate-phosphate buffer","citrate–phosphate (CP) buffer"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"obi","ontology_prefix":"OBI","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000149","ontology_name":"mesh","related_synonyms":["Acid Phosphate Fluoride","Fluoride, Acid Phosphate","Fluoride, Acidulated Phosphate","Phosphate Fluoride, Acidulated"],"ontology_prefix":"mesh","short_form":"mesh_D000149","description":["A sodium fluoride solution, paste or powder, which has been acidulated to pH 3 to 4 and buffered with a phosphate. It is used in the prevention of dental caries."],"label":"Acidulated Phosphate Fluoride","obo_id":"mesh:D000149","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MSIO_0000021","ontology_name":"msio","ontology_prefix":"MSIO","short_form":"MSIO_0000021","description":["Phosphated buffer saline (PBS) buffer is a buffer which is a water-based salt solution containing disodium hydrogen phosphate, sodium chloride and, in some formulations, potassium chloride and potassium dihydrogen phosphate."],"label":"PBS buffer","obo_id":"MSIO:0000021","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C208417","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C208417","description":["A measure of alkaline phosphatase concentration in blood. It is defined as the quantity of alkaline phosphatase that releases 1 mg of phosphate ion during the first hour of incubation with a buffered substrate containing sodium beta-glycerophosphate."],"label":"Bodansky Unit","obo_id":"NCIT:C208417","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Bodansky Unit","Bodansky unit","Bodansky","[bdsk\u0027U]","bdsk\u0027U"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/XCO_0000116","ontology_name":"xco","related_synonyms":["Krebs-Henseleit buffer perfusate","Krebs-Henseleit solution perfusate","Krebs-Ringer buffer perfusate","Krebs-Ringer solution perfusate"],"ontology_prefix":"XCO","short_form":"XCO_0000116","description":["A buffered, aqueous solution usually containing the cations sodium, potassium, calcium and magnesium, and anions chloride, sulfate, bicarbonate and phosphate and often including glucose as an energy source which is injected or pumped into, or poured through, an organ or tissue, usually via a blood vessel."],"label":"Kreb\u0027s solution perfusate","obo_id":"XCO:0000116","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/XCO_0000146","ontology_name":"xco","related_synonyms":["controlled oxygen content Krebs-Henseleit buffer perfusate","controlled oxygen content Krebs-Henseleit solution perfusate","controlled oxygen content Krebs-Ringer buffer perfusate","controlled oxygen content Krebs-Ringer solution perfusate"],"ontology_prefix":"XCO","short_form":"XCO_0000146","description":["A buffered, aqueous solution usually containing the cations sodium, potassium, calcium and magnesium, and anions chloride, sulfate, bicarbonate and phosphate and often including glucose as an energy source in which a specified amount of the tasteless, odorless, colorless gas essential for aerobic respiration with atomic number 8 has been dissolved, which is injected or pumped into, or poured through, an organ or tissue, usually via a blood vessel."],"label":"controlled oxygen content Kreb\u0027s solution perfusate","obo_id":"XCO:0000146","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C150398","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C150398","description":["A gel composed of the sodium succinate form of the glucocorticoid hydrocortisone mixed with aluminum phosphate, with potential protective activity. Upon oral administration of the hydrocortisone sodium succinate/aluminum phosphate gel, the gel forms a layer over the esophageal mucosa, which may restore and protect the esophageal membrane against damage. Hydrocortisone exerts anti-inflammatory effects locally, may reduce or prevent infection, may reduce the formation of connective tissue in order to prevent postoperative esophageal stenosis and stricture, and may reduce symptoms of dysphagia or choking, after endoscopic submucosal dissection (ESD). The aluminum phosphate acts as a buffer and may protect the local mucosal membrane from the acidic environment."],"label":"Hydrocortisone Sodium Succinate/Aluminum Phosphate Gel","obo_id":"NCIT:C150398","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Hydrocortisone Sodium Succinate Mixed with Aluminum Phosphate Gel","Hydrocortisone Sodium Succinate/Aluminum Phosphate Gel"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"micro","ontology_prefix":"MICRO","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"one","ontology_prefix":"ONE","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0100046","ontology_name":"vo","ontology_prefix":"VO","short_form":"OBI_0100046","description":["Phosphate buffered saline (abbreviated PBS) is a buffer solution commonly used in biochemistry. It is a salty solution containing sodium chloride, sodium phosphate and in some preparations potassium chloride and potassium phosphate. The buffer helps to maintain a constant pH. The concentration usually matches the human body (isotonic)."],"label":"phosphate buffered saline solution","obo_id":"OBI:0100046","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_37585","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"CHEBI_37585","description":["LanguaL term definition: Food additive; technological purpose(s): acidity regulator, buffer, emulsifier, humectant, moisture-retention agent, raising agent, sequestrant, stabilizer, texturizing agent."],"label":"sodium dihydrogenphosphate","obo_id":"CHEBI:37585","type":"class"}],"numFound":14,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["XCO","3","NCIT","2","CHMO","2","MICRO","1","MSIO","1","FOODON","1","OBI","1","ONE","1","VO","1","mesh","1"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","10","false","4"],"ontologyId":["xco","3","ncit","2","chmo","2","micro","1","msio","1","foodon","1","obi","1","one","1","vo","1","mesh","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/xco.owl","3","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/chmo.owl","2","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/msio.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ONE","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/vo.owl","1","https://w3id.org/biopragmatics/resources/mesh/mesh.ofn","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/foodon.owl","1","http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MicrO.owl","1"],"isObsolete":["false","14"],"type":["class","14"]}}}